<article class="env-lemma" id="03XN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03XN">Lemma <span data-tag="03XN">67.27.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X \to Y \to Z$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $X \to Z$ is locally quasi-finite, then $X \to Y$ is locally quasi-finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[d] \ar[r] &  V \ar[d] \ar[r] &  W \ar[d] \\  X \ar[r] &  Y \ar[r] &  Z }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with vertical arrows étale and surjective. (See Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02X1" data-tag="02X1">65.11.6</a>.) Apply Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/03WR" data-tag="03WR">29.21.17</a> to the top row. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>